  "description": "Pickle brine, lemon juice, and smoky mezcal combine in this marriage of pickle lemonade and hard lemonade that’s sharp, salty, and just sweet enough.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Dill pickles, thinly sliced lengthwise for serving (optional); Lemon slices for serving (optional); Soda water for serving (optional)\n\nNotes: While I love the smoky flavor mezcal gives this lemonade, vodka, gin, tequila blanco, and even whiskey also work well if you want to spike the drink.\nThis recipe reflects my preferred balance of pickle brine, lemonade, and water for a sweet-tart drink. You can adjust the proportions with additional water, lemon juice, or pickle brine to suit your own taste, keeping in mind that the lemonade will dilute further when served over ice.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The lemonade can be refrigerated in an airtight container for a week, though I'd remove the lemon rounds after a day, as they can make the drink bitter.",
